{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#138","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#138","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#138\",\"parent_revision\":\"ba2a3b8f16ca870fff26b1c01888e25ea06d56afe65ce723246e9bda2fb73294\",\"root_revision\":\"ba2a3b8f16ca870fff26b1c01888e25ea06d56afe65ce723246e9bda2fb73294\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nOn the `claude_code` path a `SKILL.md` with no `name` is reported twice:\\n\\n- **AS001** as an **error** \u2014 agentskills.io requires the field\\n- **FM001** as a **warning** \u2014 `skills.md` calls it optional\\n\\nTwo rules, one condition, opposite severities. Pre-existing on `main`.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Why It Was Not Fixed In 102\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nThat PR avoided introducing the duplicate on the shared path by filtering FM001 to its description claim, but the pipeline duplicate remains.\\n\\nResolving it means answering a design question rather than editing code: **which spec does the FM series answer to when agentskills.io and `skills.md` disagree?** That decision belongs with #112's provenance work.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Related\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- #112 \u2014 rule provenance architecture\\n- #132 \u2014 the same \\\"which spec governs\\\" question for `skills` on agent files\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"a4ba9d15f0f004bcf596c12a98360b8021b5e648c65a5fe7e6ae92ceaf2592de\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDORXxKvc8AAAABShvFzw\"}"}